# A server that accepts outside a parallel group.
#
# Should: wait for a connection, then answer it. Start it, then run
#   curl -s localhost:48219/
# from another shell and see "hi".
#
# Does: exits at once on every engine with
#   error[endpoint]: unhandled err reached the executor: "nothing connected"
# The executor's accept assumes that only another fiber of the same program
# could ever connect, so with no group around it there is nothing to wait
# for. Putting `serve l` in a group with any other statement makes it work.
import "./solo"
import "std/net"

net/listen 48219 .> solo/serve
